a:["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-2","children":[["$","section",null,{"id":"introduction","className":"scroll-mt-20 border-t border-border pt-12 first:border-0 first:pt-0","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-link","children":"Overview"}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl","children":"Introduction"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-5 space-y-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-secondary","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"shadw turns any machine you run into a region. Nodes find each other over a real peer-to-peer mesh (Iroh QUIC, with NAT traversal + relay fallback) and serve your deployments by anycast — no data center, no public IPs. The platform is two layers over one isolation backend:"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5","children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-fg","children":"Builds"}]," — turn a git repo into build output (framework detection or a Dockerfile)."]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-fg","children":"Fluid compute"}]," — serve functions on long-lived instances that handle many concurrent requests, autoscale, and scale to zero."]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":["Everything below talks to the platform ",["$","strong",null,{"className":"text-fg","children":"API"}]," at ",["$","code",null,{"className":"rounded bg-subtle px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.85em] text-fg","children":"https://api.shadw.cloud"}],". (Self-hosting? The same endpoints live on your node's admin API — default ",["$","code",null,{"className":"rounded bg-subtle px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.85em] text-fg","children":"127.0.0.1:8786"}],".)"]}]]}]]}],["$","section",null,{"id":"quickstart","className":"scroll-mt-20 border-t border-border pt-12 first:border-0 first:pt-0","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-link","children